<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Moresby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded <a href="/years/1873">1873</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port Moresby is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>, on the south coast of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>. Named in 1873 by the British naval officer John Moresby, it was the seat of British New Guinea from 1884 and then of the Australian Territory of Papua. A major Allied base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, it became the capital of independent Papua New Guinea in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-moresby.jpg" alt="Port Moresby" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MSchlauch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Moresby_Town2_Mschlauch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In November 1884 Commodore James Erskine proclaimed a British protectorate over the southeast at <b>Port Moresby</b>, days after Germany had raised its flag over the north, which became German New Guinea.</blockquote><a href="/state/british-new-guinea">British New Guinea</a></li><li><blockquote>Britain transferred British New Guinea to the new Commonwealth of Australia, and the Papua Act of 1905, in force from 1906, renamed it the Territory of Papua, with its capital at <b>Port Moresby</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/territory-of-papua">Territory of Papua</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Second World War Australia combined the Territory of Papua and the Territory of New Guinea under the Papua and New Guinea Act of 1949, with a single administrator at <b>Port Moresby</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/territory-of-papua-and-new-guinea">Territory of Papua and New Guinea</a></li></ul></section>
